sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (browser)
    participant W as Next.js (web :3000)
    participant A as API /api/v1/auth
    participant L as Login rate limiter<br/>(in-process per worker: 5/min per<br/>client IP + email AND 10/min per email)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (users)

    U->>W: GET /customers (no cookie)
    W-->>U: 307 -> /login (middleware.ts route guard)
    U->>W: POST /api/v1/auth/login {email, password}
    W->>A: proxied (rewrite), same origin
    A->>A: Pydantic LoginRequest (trim + lower-case email, length bounds)
    A->>L: hit(ip|email) and hit(email)
    alt over 5 per (IP, email) or 10 per email within 60 s
        L-->>A: retry_after (either budget exhausted)
        A-->>U: 429 RATE_LIMITED (error envelope + request_id)
    end
    A->>DB: SELECT user WHERE email = lower(:email)
    DB-->>A: user row or none
    A->>A: Argon2id verify (dummy hash if user unknown = same cost)
    alt unknown user / wrong password / inactive
        A-->>U: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS (one message for all three)
    else valid
        A->>L: reset both budgets
        A->>DB: UPDATE last_login_at (+ rehash if params changed), then COMMIT
        A->>A: issue JWT HS256 {sub, role, iat, exp=+60 min, iss}
        A-->>W: 200 {user, expires_at} + Set-Cookie finpilot_session<br/>HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, Secure (when HTTPS)
        W-->>U: response passes through, token never in body or JS
    end
    Note over U,A: Every later request: cookie -> decode (alg pinned, iss/exp/iat/sub/role required)<br/>-> users re-read by PK -> 401 SESSION_EXPIRED if missing/inactive -> role check (403)